# The upper-form files this module keeps but does not build.
#
# Each of these stands in for a rule IBM itself compiled. They are here so
# that tools/upper-check.sh has an authored rule to hold against the one it
# replaces, which is how the compiler is proved at all; building them would
# put our bytecode where IBM's is and give up the byte identity English is
# checked by. A module written rather than lifted names nothing here, because
# every rule in the upper form is its own.

es_cdur.up
et_prfx.up
u_integ.up
ut_main.up
